<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Javonte Green Paid $3.94m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Green is paid <strong>$3.94m</strong> because eight seasons of doing a narrow job well is worth something, and the minimum rises with years of service whatever else happens.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went undrafted in 2015 and did not play an NBA game until 2019.</li>
<li>He has signed nine NBA contracts, two of them ten-day or rest-of-season deals worth under <strong>$140k</strong>.</li>
<li>He has signed for six clubs.</li>
<li>Two of his eight seasons published no salary figure at all.</li>
<li>He defends, cuts and finishes, and has never taken many shots.</li>
</ul>
<p>He is 33 and this is the first season he has been paid more than <strong>$3.5m</strong>.</p>

